You are a senior frontend engineer and UI/UX designer.

Build a WhatsApp-style chat application layout in React with Tailwind CSS.
Focus on the full two-column layout — sidebar on the left, chat window 
on the right. Production-quality code, not a tutorial prototype.

---

## Overall Layout

Desktop (≥768px):
- Fixed full-height two-column layout (no page scroll)
- Left sidebar: exactly 340px wide, fixed height, internal scroll
- Right panel: fills remaining width, fixed height, internal scroll
- No gap between sidebar and chat panel

Mobile (<768px):
- Sidebar and chat panel are separate full-screen views
- Sidebar is the default view
- Clicking a chat slides in the chat panel (CSS transition)
- Back button in chat header returns to sidebar

---

## Left Sidebar

### Top header bar
- Left: app logo or name ("ChatApp")
- Right: two icon buttons — new chat (pencil icon), menu (three dots)
- Height: 60px
- Bottom border separating from content below

### Search bar
- Full width, below header
- Rounded pill input with search icon on the left inside
- Placeholder: "Search or start new chat"
- Padding: 8px 16px
- Filters chat list in real time as user types

### Chat list
- Scrollable independently (overflow-y: auto)
- Takes all remaining sidebar height below search

Each chat list item (72px tall):
- Left: circular avatar (40px), initials fallback if no photo,
  small green online dot overlaid on bottom-right of avatar
- Middle: 
  - Top row: contact name (bold, 15px) + timestamp (small, gray, right-aligned)
  - Bottom row: last message preview (13px, gray, truncated) + 
    unread count badge (green circle, right-aligned, hidden if 0)
- States:
  - Default: white background
  - Hover: #F0F2F5 background, smooth transition
  - Active/selected: #F0F2F5 background, left accent border (3px green)
- Clicking sets this chat as active in the right panel

---

## Right Panel — Chat Window

### Chat header (60px tall)
- Left: avatar (40px) + contact name (bold) + status line 
  ("online" in green, or "last seen today at 3:42 PM" in gray)
- Right: icon buttons — video call, phone call, search, three dots menu
- Bottom border separating from message area

### Message area
- Takes all space between header and input bar
- Scrollable independently
- Background color: #ECE5DD (WhatsApp beige) in light mode,
  #0B141A in dark mode
- Newest messages at the bottom
- Auto-scrolls to bottom when new message arrives
- If user scrolled up and new message arrives:
  show floating pill button "1 new message ↓" at bottom center

### Date dividers
Between messages from different days:
- Centered gray pill label: "Today", "Yesterday", or "Mon, 12 May"
- Subtle background, small text (12px)

### Message bubbles

Sent (right-aligned):
- Background: #DCF8C6 (light green) / #005C4B dark mode
- Max width: 65% of message area
- Border radius: 8px, bottom-right corner 2px (WhatsApp tail effect)
- Content: message text + timestamp (11px, gray, bottom-right) + 
  read receipt icon (✓ gray / ✓✓ gray / ✓✓ blue)
- No avatar shown

Received (left-aligned):
- Background: white / #1F2C34 dark mode
- Same max width and radius, bottom-left corner 2px
- Avatar shown to the left of bubble (only on last message in a group)

Grouping rules:
- Consecutive messages from same sender within 5 minutes = a group
- Within a group: no avatar repeat, reduced top margin (2px instead of 8px)
- Last message in group gets the tail corner effect
- Non-last messages: fully rounded

### Input bar (60px tall)
- Full width, fixed to bottom of right panel
- Top border or subtle shadow
- Left icons: emoji button, attachment (paperclip) button
- Center: rounded pill input, placeholder "Type a message"
- Right: when input empty → microphone icon button
         when input has text → green circle send button (white arrow icon)
- Pressing Enter sends the message
- After sending: input clears, message appears, panel scrolls to bottom

